  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Let the four boxes be Box-1, Box-2, Box-3 and Box-4. Each of the box has&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;red balls and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;blue balls.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0004_228b5befb9d8.png\" style=\"width: 475px; height: 200px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math>&nbsp;balls can be chosen in:</p><p>Case I - When exactly one box gives four balls</p><p>Case II - When exactly two boxes gives three balls</p><p>Required number of ways<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo></math>&nbsp;Number of ways in Case I&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo></math> Number of ways in Case II.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>4</mn></mmultiscripts><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>2</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>+</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>3</mn></mmultiscripts></mrow></mfenced><msup><mfenced><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>3</mn></mmultiscripts><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>2</mn></mmultiscripts></mrow></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>4</mn></mmultiscripts><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>3</mn></mmultiscripts><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>2</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>+</mo><mmultiscripts>